            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "What exactly was failing?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
                        "email": "molberding@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "molbear"
                    },
                    "message": "the file lookup for the schema. It assumed that for a given node's Type parameter, there exists a file with the name put to lower case, which isn't true for many record types, maybe it was true at some point. If thats the expectation, we need to go fix schema files."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
                        "email": "molberding@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "molbear"
                    },
                    "message": "it turns out this is just completely broken, top to bottom. In order to make this API work, I'm considering just skipping schema validation, because the whole validation feature is broken."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/dbus_interface.cpp",
                    "line": 258,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "nit: extra newline diff"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/dbus_interface.cpp",
                    "line": 258,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
                        "email": "molberding@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "molbear"
                    },
                    "message": "ack, will fix on the next uprev."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/dbus_interface.cpp",
                    "line": 258,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
                        "email": "molberding@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "molbear"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/dbus_interface.cpp",
                    "line": 334,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Did you enable `ENABLE_RUNTIME_VALIDATE_JSON` and test with that?\n\nSince `global.json` is for EM config files, adding a single record such as with `AddObject` should fail to validate, right?\n\nShould we validate against `schemas/exposes_record.json` instead?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/dbus_interface.cpp",
                    "line": 334,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
                        "email": "molberding@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "molbear"
                    },
                    "message": "good point, I'll test with schemas/exposes_record.json, as well as double check that ENABLE_RUNTIME_VALIDATE_JSON is enabled during the test."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/dbus_interface.cpp",
                    "line": 334,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "> ENABLE_RUNTIME_VALIDATE_JSON\n\nConsidering that this option has never worked since inception, I'm not going to start requiring people test against it.  If we get to the point where it could be generally enabled without harm, we can have a different discussion, but asking someone to test an option that we KNOW doesn't work it haphazard."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/dbus_interface.cpp",
                    "line": 334,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
                        "email": "molberding@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "molbear"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
